698 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 310 0 R
/E (      Voice-based educational and online examination systems can also integrate features such as automatic question randomization, time management alerts, and instant scoring, making assessments more secure and efficient for institutions while remaining accessible to visually impaired learners. These platforms often support multiple languages and subject formats \(objective, descriptive, and oral responses\), allowing students to participate in a wide range of academic activities using only their voice.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
699 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 310 0 R
/E (     In addition, some systems store performance data and generate progress reports, helping teachers and parents monitor learning outcomes without requiring separate, specialized tools. When combined with user authentication \(like voice profiles or PINs\), these platforms can maintain exam integrity while still offering a fully audio-driven experience, bridging the gap between accessibility and academic rigor for visually impaired students.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
